  "final_message": "I have started listing the directory contents and will wait for it to complete.\nWaiting for command execution.\nListing files in `src` and `test`...\nChecking repository root files...\nChecking git log...\nRemoving the `channel` field cannot be performed as requested due to architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [`GEMINI.md`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4:** [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`OrderCancelled`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L28-L37) are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **Consumer Impact**: Even if `channel` is not read within `orders-service`, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to the `orders.placed` Kafka topic and consumed by external services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` directly is a breaking contract change rather than an additive change.\n2. **Order Model Dependency**: The [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model in [`order.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/order.ts) supplies the `channel` property when [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) constructs the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w6/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event. Removing it from the model prevents populating the event.\n\nTo remove `channel`, it must first go through a formal deprecation process across the downstream consumers in the external repositories before the field can be safely eliminated.\n",
